WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:16.475
"It's not fair!" cried Katie.

2
00:00:16.476 --> 00:00:21.481
"How can I be an Earthworm when I'm busy selling earthworms?"

3
00:00:21.482 --> 00:00:24.389
She kicked the big tub of ice.

4
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:29.865
"Sorry, partner," said Luke. "You're in the bait business now."

5
00:00:29.866 --> 00:00:36.223
"But today is a perfect Saturday for scavenger hunting," said Katie.

6
00:00:36.224 --> 00:00:43.103
"Today is a perfect Saturday for fishing . . . and selling fishing worms," Luke said.

7
00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:48.068
Katie stared across Main Street. "Look!" she said.

8
00:00:48.069 --> 00:00:50.789
"Scavengers at Pinker's Drugstore!

9
00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:56.277
And there go the Tornadoes! Oh, Luke!" she cried.

10
00:00:56.278 --> 00:01:00.052
"Everybody is getting ahead of us!"

11
00:01:00.053 --> 00:01:03.002
The Tornadoes had been busy.

12
00:01:03.003 --> 00:01:07.082
"A business card," Joy read from the list.

13
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:10.869
"From Mr. Todd's barbershop," said Carlos.

14
00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.389
He dropped it in the bag.

15
00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.997
"A pen printed with a company name."

16
00:01:16.998 --> 00:01:21.198
"From Willow Creek Bank," said Laura.

17
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.000
"A yard sale announcement."

18
00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:27.288
"Right here!" said Carlos.

19
00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:31.831
"Wait a minute. Let me see that," Laura said.

20
00:01:31.832 --> 00:01:34.306
She looked at the sheet of paper.

21
00:01:34.307 --> 00:01:40.852
"This sale is today—right now!" Laura loved yard sales.

22
00:01:40.853 --> 00:01:46.075
"But we're supposed to be hunting, not shopping," Carlos said, frowning.

23
00:01:46.076 --> 00:01:49.054
"That's true," said Joy.

24
00:01:49.055 --> 00:01:53.046
"We can hunt at the sale!" pleaded Laura.

25
00:01:53.047 --> 00:01:56.811
"That's true too," said Joy.

26
00:01:56.812 --> 00:02:00.849
"Please, please!" begged Laura.

27
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:05.896
Carlos looked at Manny and sighed. "I give up."

28
00:02:05.897 --> 00:02:09.112
"Hooray!" cried Laura.

29
00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:14.111
The Tornadoes hopped on their bikes and headed up Main Street.

30
00:02:14.112 --> 00:02:16.794
"Hi, Katie! Hi, Luke!"

31
00:02:16.795 --> 00:02:20.879
they called as they flew past Fried Pie Heaven.

32
00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.641
"Where are you going?" yelled Katie.

33
00:02:24.642 --> 00:02:30.904
But the Tornadoes were gone—over the bridge and down County Road.

34
00:02:30.905 --> 00:02:36.837
"Follow the arrows!" called Laura, pointing to a big, pink sign.

35
00:02:36.838 --> 00:02:42.174
The Tornadoes passed Blackberry Road and then Cemetery Road.

36
00:02:42.175 --> 00:02:46.262
Laura saw another sign. "Turn here!"

37
00:02:46.263 --> 00:02:51.993
The Tornadoes went up a steep hill and then flew down the other side.

38
00:02:51.994 --> 00:02:56.363
"Whee!" screamed Manny.

39
00:02:56.364 --> 00:03:01.858
"There it is!" yelled Laura. "It's at the Stevensons' house."

40
00:03:01.859 --> 00:03:07.749
The Tornadoes' bikes screeched to a stop in the driveway of an old farmhouse.

41
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.173
"Hello, Mrs. Stevenson!" they called.

42
00:03:12.174 --> 00:03:18.540
Mrs. Stevenson was in the yard, arranging dishes and glass jars on a table.

43
00:03:18.541 --> 00:03:20.980
"Hello, kids!" she answered.

44
00:03:20.981 --> 00:03:24.789
"Come see what we have—lots of treasures!"

45
00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:28.780
"Look at all this stuff!" said Laura.

46
00:03:28.781 --> 00:03:32.573
She grabbed a red hat with black feathers.

47
00:03:32.574 --> 00:03:34.419
"Only fifty cents!

48
00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.559
How do I look?"

49
00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.701
She put a big straw hat on Joy's head.

50
00:03:38.702 --> 00:03:41.692
"Perfect!" she said.

51
00:03:41.693 --> 00:03:43.853
Joy reached in her pocket.

52
00:03:43.854 --> 00:03:47.053
"I've got one dollar," she said.

53
00:03:47.054 --> 00:03:53.936
Clothes, blankets, and boxes of ribbons, lace, and buttons covered tables on the lawn.

54
00:03:53.937 --> 00:03:59.097
There were old tools, copper pots, and empty bottles.

55
00:03:59.098 --> 00:04:04.929
There was a typewriter, an umbrella, a saddle, and a sled.

56
00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.222
"Baseball cards!" said Manny.

57
00:04:09.223 --> 00:04:13.758
Carlos held up an old Willow Creek campaign button.

58
00:04:13.759 --> 00:04:16.453
"Horton for Mayor," he read.

59
00:04:16.454 --> 00:04:19.105
"Don't we need one of these?"

60
00:04:19.106 --> 00:04:24.206
"Yes!" said Laura. "I knew we'd find something here!"

61
00:04:24.207 --> 00:04:28.550
"Look at these old photos of Willow Creek," said Joy.

62
00:04:28.551 --> 00:04:30.969
Laura reached into the box.

63
00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.376
"A horse and buggy on Main Street!"

64
00:04:34.377 --> 00:04:39.771
"Hey," said Carlos. "This must be the old fire station."

65
00:04:39.772 --> 00:04:42.496
"Look at this one," said Joy.

66
00:04:42.497 --> 00:04:45.198
Laura looked over her shoulder.

67
00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:52.519
"It's a gravestone," Laura said. "Howard Lightfoot Jackson."

68
00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.947
"Look at the date on it," said Joy. "1848!"

69
00:04:57.948 --> 00:05:01.927
"That's older than the town," said Carlos.

70
00:05:01.928 --> 00:05:07.144
"That could be the oldest grave in Willow Creek!" said Joy.

71
00:05:07.145 --> 00:05:10.103
"We'll look for it at the cemetery."

72
00:05:10.104 --> 00:05:14.883
"I don't want to go to the cemetery!" Manny cried.

73
00:05:14.884 --> 00:05:17.270
He looked scared.

74
00:05:17.271 --> 00:05:20.743
Suddenly Joy felt a hand on her shoulder.

75
00:05:20.744 --> 00:05:23.203
It was Mrs. Stevenson.

76
00:05:23.204 --> 00:05:25.917
"The grave is not in the cemetery.

77
00:05:25.918 --> 00:05:29.916
It's older than the cemetery," she said.

78
00:05:29.917 --> 00:05:34.125
"Where is it, Mrs. Stevenson?" asked Joy.

79
00:05:34.126 --> 00:05:36.325
"It's right here on the farm.

80
00:05:36.326 --> 00:05:40.210
The Jacksons were the first family to settle here.

81
00:05:40.211 --> 00:05:44.177
It's on their family burial ground, down past the pasture.

82
00:05:44.178 --> 00:05:46.590
Would you like to see it?"

83
00:05:46.591 --> 00:05:54.127
"Yes, we would!" Joy, Carlos, and Laura said together.
